      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the value of \\(4^4 \\cdot 5^4\\), we can use the property of exponents that states \\((a \\cdot b)^n = a^n \\cdot b^n\\). Here, we can let \\(a = 4\\) and \\(b = 5\\), and \\(n = 4\\). Applying the property, we get:\n\n\\[\n4^4 \\cdot 5^4 = (4 \\cdot 5)^4\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the product inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n4 \\cdot 5 = 20\n\\]\n\nSo, the expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n(4 \\cdot 5)^4 = 20^4\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to calculate \\(20^4\\). We can do this step by step:\n\n\\[\n20^2 = 20 \\cdot 20 = 400\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\(20^4\\) by squaring \\(20^2\\):\n\n\\[\n20^4 = (20^2)^2 = 400^2\n\\]\n\nTo find \\(400^2\\), we can break it down as follows:\n\n\\[\n400^2 = (400 \\cdot 400) = 160000\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(4^4 \\cdot 5^4\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{160000}\n\\]",
